# Architecture

## Top-level layout

| Path                                | Contents                                                            |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/`                              | The `dx*` command entry points (`dxf.ts`, `dxi.ts`, `dxr.ts`)       |
| `src/lib/`                          | `xProcess` and supporting library modules                           |
| `tests/`                            | `deno test` suites; `00.project.*.test.ts` are the CI project gates |
| `tests/fixtures/`, `tests/helpers/` | Test data and helpers                                               |
| `eg/`                               | Example scripts (with and without `xProcess`) for manual comparison |
| `bench/`                            | Benchmarks (run via `dxr`)                                          |
| `tools/`                            | Maintenance scripts, incl. shim-revision prototypes                 |
| `vendor/`                           | Vendored dependencies — do not edit                                 |
| `.changelog/`                       | `git-changelog` templates                                           |
| `.tasks/`                           | Scripts backing `deno task` entries                                 |

## `dx*` commands (`src/`)

- `dxf.ts` — detects `dprint` + config in the project root; runs `dprint fmt`, otherwise `deno fmt`.
- `dxi.ts` — installs a script with an enhanced shim; shim adds bash-like arg/brace/glob expansion on Windows and blocks the batch-interrupt prompt.
- `dxr.ts` — runs a target script applying the same expansion while preserving quote semantics; also improves `$0`/`%0` for `xProcess` scripts.
- `dxx.ts` — integrator, WIP.

## Key `src/lib/` modules

| Module                                   | Role                                                       |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `xProcess.ts`                            | Main library: recover true invocation text + expanded args |
| `xArgs.ts`                               | Argument tokenizing / expansion                            |
| `xBraces.ts`                             | Brace expansion                                            |
| `xFetch.ts`                              | Fetch helpers                                              |
| `xWalk.ts`                               | Filesystem walking                                         |
| `commandLine.ts`                         | Command-line reconstruction (esp. Windows)                 |
| `shim.windows.ts`                        | Windows shim generation                                    |
| `consoleSize.ts`, `consoleSizeViaFFI.ts` | Terminal size detection (incl. optional FFI path)          |
| `restyleYargsHelp.ts`                    | Help-text formatting                                       |
| `eol.ts`, `utils.ts`                     | Misc helpers                                               |
| `$deps.ts`, `$deps.cli.ts`               | Central dependency re-exports                              |
| `$shared.ts`, `$shared.TLA.ts`           | Shared runtime helpers (TLA = top-level await variant)     |

## How the pieces fit

Scripts get enhanced argument handling three ways: (1) run through `dxr`, (2) installed with `dxi`'s enhanced shim, or (3) `--unstable` FFI. `xProcess` reads whichever context is available to present accurate args and invocation text, which also lets `deno compile` produce fully self-contained binaries.
